# What graphify indexes: the library source, and nothing else. Committed, and read
# by both `extract` and `update`, so a fresh clone -- which is what CI and the
# weekly drift job are -- rebuilds the same graph as a working checkout. The
# `--code-only` scope lives in an untracked cache and would not survive the trip.

# Configuration and prose: mapping keys and headings, not structure. The CI
# workflows alone were 533 of the 8791 nodes in the unscoped survey graph.
*.yml
*.yaml
*.md
*.rst
*.txt
*.svg
*.png

# Project metadata. Also stops a dependency bump from moving the graph: every
# pyproject.toml is otherwise indexed, so bumping a pin churns the committed file
# for no change in the code.
*.toml

# Tests. The 202 test modules were 3910 nodes and 11353 edges -- 44% of the
# survey graph and half its bytes -- for the one part of the tree whose layout
# is already predictable: packages/<dist>/tests mirrors packages/<dist>/src.
# Grep the tests; query the graph for the 262 modules under src/.
tests/

# Not library code: the benchmark harness, the one-off plot scripts, the Sphinx
# config and the dev-task runners. Nothing an agent navigating galax routes
# through, and the graph is a map of the library.
benchmarks/
scripts/
docs/
noxfile.py
conftest.py
